    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0423" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.00/824: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Carter</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-06-04T10:00:00-00:44">June 4, 1930—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:27 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>75. I saw President King yesterday, taking occasion to assure the President of
                    American friendship, and I stated further my assurance that the good offices of
                    the United States would be forthcoming in the present admitted crisis in the
                    event he had to call for them.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d271-f1"/></p>
                <p>He seemed to appreciate this attitude.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Carter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
